The build is failing during the devicetree processing stage. This is typically caused by an issue in a devicetree overlay file that violates the device's bindings.

Based on the bindings for `zephyr,dac-emulator`, the `label` property is required for each device instance. The provided overlay file `tests/drivers/dac/dac_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay` is missing this property for all three defined nodes.

The fix is to add a unique `label` property to each of the `dac-emulator` nodes.

tests/drivers/dac/dac_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
/ {
	dac_emul0: dac-emulator@0 {
		compatible = "zephyr,dac-emulator";
		nchannels = <4>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};

	dac_emul_unconfigured: dac-emulator@1 {
		compatible = "zephyr,dac-emulator";
		nchannels = <1>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};

	dac_emul_many: dac-emulator@2 {
		compatible = "zephyr,dac-emulator";
		nchannels = <16>;
		#io-channel-cells = <1>;
		status = "okay";
	};
};
========
